																		Jeanne&#039;s Home for Strange and Lost Creatures
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ohthehumanity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6183720); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6183720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607914697" alt="OhTheHumanity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6183720)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ohthehumanity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6183720); return false;" >OhTheHumanity</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607007502 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Dec 2020 14:58</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835229">
									

<p>An anomalous house with an anomalous family- they came together because of a mysterious call. And new members are still coming.</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong><br />
- House description</p>
<p>- Experiments with the house</p>
<p>- Jeanne description, interview</p>
<p>- Event: New family member arrives</p>
<p>- Jeanne post-event interview</p>
<p>- Notes on the house's other residents</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> At its core, Jeanne's Home for Strange and Lost Creatures is intended to be proof that the anomalous isn't always sinister or scary. The Home is a group of varying anomalous individuals who live together in a &quot;bigger-on-the-inside,&quot; sentient house. The Foundation has secured the property but has established that the Home poses a minimal threat.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The overall story of Jeanne's Home for Strange and Lost Creatures is that is a tight-knit community of anomalous individuals that does not much appreciate outsiders, namely the Foundation, encroaching on it. This is characterized by the initial hostility that the Wooden Marionette expresses, That Other Guy's continued refusal to reveal himself to Foundation Scientists, and the foreboding noises coming from the Dream Garden. The house, and its residents, put up with the Foundation's presence because they don't want to give up what they have. It is loosely implied, but not confirmed, that Dr. John Hammond (The lead Foundation scientist at the Home) is developing feelings for Jeanne, the owner of the home.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The concept of a benevolent anomaly that attracts and gathers others around it is something I haven't seen before. Each resident is unique, and the main purpose of that was to humanize each of the anomalies and prove that sometimes SCPs can be people, too. Jeanne's Home for Strange and Lost Creatures is a prime example of humanity's ability to develop bonds even in the coldest and most sterile circumstances.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The Home was originally created as a fan-piece for the Unfounded canon, as a place where some of the more overtly anomalous beings could live in safety. The title &quot;Jeanne's Home for Strange and Lost Creatures&quot; is a nod to a children's book, written by Ben Hatke, of a similar name.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
