<p>Lots of potential here! You're carving out a very ambitious scope but it sounds like you have the momentum to deliver on it. The creepy/chilling part here would perhaps come in where the Foundation tries to contain all these free entities living in peace. The potential for an Ethics Committee rationale par-excellance seems to be a likely ending that would make it sing.</p>
<p>What's your take on 239? This is is a bit like 239 x 5.</p>
<p>What are the characters' names, personalities, ages?<br />
Are they choleric, sanguine, phlegmatic or melancholic? You can pull off an ensemble effect if you array them all.</p>
<p>What are their DnD alignments?</p>
<p>What do they look like?</p>
<p>What are their wardrobe choices and how do these reflect their character? (maybe too much detail for a file but ok for a Tale or offset).</p>
<p>How are the relations between the characters? Do they like each other?</p>
<p>In what state are the characters at the start, happy-ish right?</p>
<p>What change triggers the story? Where and what exactly is the point of no return (nothing will ever be the same). How does this change the characters? Do they turn violent? Does the case researcher lose faith in the Foundation by the end?</p>
<p>Does the exploration log of the MTF deployed to take them in have anything reminiscent of war crimes commited in Iraq (or many other places)?</p>

