			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842331">
									

<p>I said I would write a small description of each of the residents, and after a small amount of procrastination I delivered! Here you go!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Jeanne</p>
<p>Quick description: Caucasion, red hair, brown eyes. Lots of freckles. She seems to be able to suppress other anomalous abilities.</p>
<p>Personality type: Choleric-Phlegmatic</p>
<p>Personality description: “Group Mom.” Takes things she considers her duty really seriously.</p>
<p>Glass Kitten (Pepper)<br />
Quick description: A living cat that by all accounts seems to be made out of glass.</p>
<p>Personality type: Cat</p>
<p>Personality description: Cat</p>
<p>Wooden Marionette (&quot;Mendigo&quot;)<br />
Quick description: A large wooden marionette with brass rings for joints. It is capable of taking itself apart to avoid capture, and is remarkably strong. Speaks through sign language usually.</p>
<p>Personality type: Melancholic-Plegmatic</p>
<p>Personality description: A quiet protector. Enjoys nature. Dry sense of humor. Slow to anger but when he’s pissed, he’s pissed.</p>
<p>Clockwork Dragon (&quot;Dragon&quot;)<br />
Description: A tiny, sentient dragon made out of clockwork machinery. It really likes Erin and really likes sitting in sunlight.</p>
<p>Personality type: Cat</p>
<p>Personality description: Cat</p>
<p>The Triple Quartet (“Jamie, Angelica, and Erin”)<br />
Description: Jamie, Angelica, and Erin are a set of identical triplets who decline in physical and mental health the longer they are apart. When they sing together, a fourth voice is clearly audible. They have dark brown hair and blue eyes.</p>
<p>Personality types:<br />
Jamie: Sanguine<br />
Angelica: Melancholic<br />
Erin: Phlegmatic-Melancholic</p>
<p>Personality descriptions:</p>
<p>Jamie: Very much a tomboy, Jamie loves to play sports and video games. Most of her friends outside of the House are guys. The kind of teen who’ll build a treehouse on her own with no adult supervision and then put a “No dweebs allowed” sign on it.</p>
<p>Angelica: The creative type. Terrible at organization but makes some pretty great stuff. She’s friendly but she’s got to recharge her batteries every once in a while, and that means locking herself up in her room for a few hours to write or draw something.</p>
<p>Erin: A nature person, Angelica will hang out in the woods for loooong periods of time. She’s quiet but seems to understand both the Clockwork Dragon and Wooden Marionette the best. Often helps with the gardening.</p>
<p>Change (Rupert)<br />
Description: Rupert is a grizzled caucasian man with black hair and brown eyes. Prefers to cover up his skin with heavy clothes to avoid triggering his anomalous ability- any living being that he touches ages at double the normal rate. He enjoys woodworking.</p>
<p>Personality type: Choleric-Sanguine</p>
<p>Personality description: A classic “big friendly man” type. Often goes hunting to bring something special to the table. He’s the group dad but doesn’t have a romantic relationship with Jeanne.</p>
<p>True Empathy (Emily)<br />
Description: Emily is an asian girl with black hair and brown eyes. She feels the emotions and pain of anyone within a certain radius. She wants to be a doctor, no surprise there.</p>
<p>Personality type: Sanguine</p>
<p>Personality description: Emily is very outgoing and friendly. She is greatly interested in the Foundation forces present around the property and often spends time talking to the research teams and border guards. She has a tendency to be overdramatic sometimes but doesn’t do it intentionally.</p>
<p>The Dream Garden<br />
Description: The Dream Garden is a blackboard lol. The words on it can’t be erased. Anybody who falls asleep within a certain distance from it enters a lucid dream in which the dreamer is inside a magical garden. The dreams of each person affected are linked so that they can speak to each other and stuff. The Garden, being an object, doesn’t really have a personality at all lol</p>
<p>That Other Guy (Stephen)<br />
Description: W e d o n ‘ t k n o w . The guy’s almost completely invisible, being a blur in your peripheral vision at best. His voice rapidly shifts in pitch while speaking. Basically, he’s really hard to see and understand. Not a bad chef, though. If you ever see pots and pans flying around the House that’s probably him getting ready to make dinner. It is implied, but not confirmed, that he can toggle his invisibility on and off but chooses not to.</p>
<p>Personality type: Melancholic</p>
<p>Personality description: Kind of an edgy man, dislikes the Foundation forces (claiming not to trust them.) Very much a loner but he gets roped into “family activities.” When he gets comfortable with his surroundings he’s a really funny dude.</p>
<p>Sad Cloud (Anatoli)<br />
Description: Anatoli is a teen of obvious Russian descent, topped off with a faint accent to boot. His ability, when not neutralized by the house, causes anybody within a certain radius to fall into an increasingly depressive state.</p>
<p>Personality type: Sanguine through and through</p>
<p>Personality description: This is the most positive guy you’ll ever meet. He could get struck by lightning (And indeed, he has. Read Murphy’s description) and then just go “That was AWESOME! Let’s do it again!” You’d be hard-pressed to find anybody who could bring this kid down and man, people have tried. Probably the kind of guy who was legitimately hyped for Sephiroth’s appearance in Smash without even having heard of FF7.</p>
<p>Murphy's Law (Murphy)<br />
Description: Murphy is an african-american man with insanely bad luck. Fortunately, he’s invincible to everything his bad luck causes. Unfortunately, not everyone else is. He’s been hit by meteors and struck by lightning, had trees fall on him and been run over by cars. The guy’s completely fine.</p>
<p>Personality type: Melancholic</p>
<p>Personality Description: Murphy’s a pretty laid-back dude. He loves the rest of the gang and constantly provides ideas to “Murphy-proof” the house so that his ability won’t cause issues. He couldn’t care less when his bad luck bothers him, but he gets genuinely upset when his ability puts others in danger.</p>
<p>Multiple Person Disorder (Lauren)<br />
Description: Lauren is a caucasian girl. That’s the only consistent part. Her appearance changes erratically, completely altering fingerprint, skin tone, hair color, eye color, height, weight, and body type. Fortunately, it seems to change to become more useful in whatever task she’s doing at the moment. Heavy lifting results in better muscle tone, drawing results in steadier hands, etc.</p>
<p>Personality type: Choleric-Phlegmatic</p>
<p>Personality description: Lauren tries to be laid-back, taking the attitude of “it is what it is.” Despite this front, she’s terrified about her ability triggering at an inopportune moment. She’s a little bit self-absorbed as a result but she does her best to be there for her ragtag family.</p>
<p>Really Fast (Theo)<br />
Description: Theo is a young asian boy with black hair and brown eyes. He increases the flow of time around him to a factor of 3, meaning that he moves at three times the pace of a normal human and heals at the same ludicrous rate. He seems to be able to suppress his ability, though.</p>
<p>Personality type: Phlegmatic-Sanguine</p>
<p>Personality description: Theo is a really sweet kid and loves his adopted family. The little guy does his best to brighten up the lives of his fellow residents, and he usually succeeds. Despite being the baby of the crew he’s got wisdom beyond his years.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Critique welcome, looking for greenlight if possible.</p>

